{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/1507257-details-on-the-prathip-system","id":1507257,"title":"Details on the Prathip System","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","The Trinity Continuum","Trinity Continuum: \u00c6on"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-04-02T20:59:00-07:00","id":1507257,"title":"Details on the Prathip System","content":"I'm working on an Aeon game that will partially be set on a jumpship starting to explore the galaxy. Their first mission will be to survey Ribhri (from Distant Worlds, pgs 92 - 98), and as part of the background I went ahead and named the other planets in the Prathip system. I figured I'd post them here in case anyone else wants this level of crazy detail.<br /> <br /> If anyone speaks Thai and has better suggestions for the names let me know! I was just using google translate and picking words out that sparked my imagination and I had a chance of pronouncing semi-correctly, so I could riff if the players asked more questions about a specific planet. Related, if anyone knows what 'Sami' means I'd love to know. I wasn't able to find anything that made sense that sounded like 'Sami' in English.<br /> <br /> Here's my handout for the players about the star system itself.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Prath\u012bp System Data</b><br /> <br /> <b>Name</b>: Prath\u012bp (Thai for 'Lamp')<br /> <b>Star Type</b>: G2V<br /> <b>Distance from Earth</b>: 2,200 light years<br /> <b>Planets</b>: 11<ol class=\"decimal\"><li><b>Ker\u012bym</b> (Thai for 'Scorched')</li> <li><b>Kong</b> (Thai for 'Pile')</li> <li><b>Ribh\u0304r\u012b\u0300</b> (Thai for 'Glimmer')</li> <li><b>P\u0300\u0101</b> (Thai for 'Wild')</li> <li><b>M\u00e6\u0300h\u0304el\u0306k</b> (Thai for 'Magnet') - Gas Giant</li> <li><b>\u01f8\u0101</b> <b>kl\u1ea1w</b> (Thai for 'Lurid')</li> <li><b>R\u00e6nge\u0101</b> (Thai for 'Shade')</li> <li><b>Ph\u012b\u0300</b> <b>ch\u0101y</b> (Thai for 'Elder Brother') - Gas Giant</li> <li><b>Ph\u012b\u0300</b> <b>s\u0304\u0101w</b> (Thai for 'Elder Sister') - Gas Giant</li> <li><b>Ph\u0101yu</b> (Thai for 'Storm') - Gas Giant</li> <li><b>S\u0304un\u1ea1k\u0304h</b> (Thai for 'Dog')</li> </ol><b>Notes</b>: The Prath\u012bp system has a number of notable similarities to Sol. The stars are both G2V yellow dwarfs, there are the same number of gas giants, and there seems to be a cometary cloud similar to our own Oort Cloud. Ribh\u0304r\u012b\u0300 is almost the same size as earth, and is almost the same distance from Prath\u012bp as Earth is from Sol. Unlike the solar system, the orbits of six of the eleven planets in the Prath\u012bp system are notably off the solar plane by up to 13\u00ba. </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4270-literatzi","name":"literatzi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4270_2.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"177"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}